  "title": "UK inflation rises to 3.5% amid fuel price shocks and record deficits",
  "summary": "UK inflation surged to 3.5% in July, driven by energy price shocks and a record £24.5bn deficit, while the government’s debt interest payments hit record highs. The Office for National Statistics reported a CPI rise of 3.4% from August, underscoring the challenges facing consumer prices and government finances.",
