      "title": "Double blow to Healey as inflation rises to 3.5% and monthly deficit hits £24bn",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/21/inflation-rises-middle-east-conflict-drives-up-fuel-prices",
      "description": "<p>Consumer prices rise by more than expected while government’s debt interest payments surge to record high for September</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/live/2026/oct/21/uk-inflation-jump-rising-motor-fuels-cost-jackdaw-gas-field-latest-news-updates\">Business live – latest updates</a></p></li></ul><p>Inflation surged to 3.5% last month while the government deficit was a worse-than-forecast £24.5bn, in a double dose of bad news for John Healey before next week’s budget.</p><p>The Office for National Statistics said annual inflation rose <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/16/uk-inflation-rises-pressure-on-households-bank-of-england-interest-rates\">from 3.1% in August</a>, overshooting City forecasts of a rise in the consumer prices index (CPI) to 3.4%, as a result of the surging cost of fuel.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/oct/21/inflation-rises-middle-east-conflict-drives-up-fuel-prices\">Continue reading...</a>",
